7. WHAT I COULD NOT DO
================================================================================

No mtools or QEMU on this PC, so both plants ran in CI and I could not exercise
the sabotage gate locally. Did not test a real pendrive (out of scope: the stage
says STUB/UNVERIFIED, which is honest). Did not test what happens when mdir is
present but mcopy is absent (the code SKIPs that half; CI's skip rule would make
that fatal in CI).

================================================================================
8. VERDICT
================================================================================

The oracle is real and independent, and it grades what the K5a review said was
ungraded. But its verdict cannot fail the build: the stage runs in a pipeline and
every `FAILED=1` dies in the subshell, which plant G demonstrates with a green
run that printed "FAIL: USBMCOPY vs mcopy mismatch" and "check: ALL PASSED".
Until that is fixed, the K5a F1/F2 finding is closed in appearance only.

VERDICT: FAIL (F2.10-1: stage 15's failures are swallowed by the `| tee` subshell;
the oracle is sound, its enforcement is not)
